<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;I&gt;&amp;gt; , but if given a list, it should print each item with a newline.&lt;/I&gt;&lt;P&gt;


maybe changing [DOC://$,|&lt;tt&gt;$,&lt;/tt&gt;] is just good enough for your task?&lt;P&gt;

 
&lt;c&gt;
  DB&lt;223&gt; $,="\n"

  DB&lt;224&gt; @a=(); @b=1..3; $_=666

  DB&lt;225&gt; say @b
1
2
3

  DB&lt;226&gt; say @a


  DB&lt;227&gt; say
666

  DB&lt;228&gt;
&lt;/c&gt;&lt;P&gt;

But remember to use [DOC://local|&lt;tt&gt;local&lt;/tt&gt;], before changing global variables. :)&lt;P&gt;


